# Sample ECHA CLP Annex VI Table 3.1 M-factor entries.
#
# REPLACE THIS FILE with authoritative data from ECHA. The values below
# are representative placeholders for common biocide / pigment / solvent
# entries frequently seen in ink & coating catalogs, but should be
# verified against the current CLP Annex VI Table 3.1 (download from
# https://echa.europa.eu/information-on-chemicals/cl-inventory-database
# before relying on them for SDS classification).
#
# Columns:
#   cas_number         CAS Registry Number (with hyphens)
#   m_factor_acute     Acute aquatic M-factor (1, 10, 100, 1000)
#   m_factor_chronic   Chronic aquatic M-factor (1, 10, 100, 1000)
#   acute_category     Category 1 (only category with M-factor in acute)
#                      — leave blank if M-factor is chronic-only
#   chronic_category   Category 1 typically; Cat 2/3 don't carry M-factors
#                      — leave blank if M-factor is acute-only
#   source_note        Free-text provenance ("ECHA Annex VI 2024-01", etc.)
#
# Lines starting with "#" are treated as comments and skipped.
# Empty M-factor cells are treated as "not specified" (engine uses 1.0).
#
1317-38-0,10,10,Category 1,Category 1,example copper(II) oxide
7758-99-8,10,10,Category 1,Category 1,example copper sulfate pentahydrate
13463-41-7,100,100,Category 1,Category 1,example zinc pyrithione
56-35-9,1000,1000,Category 1,Category 1,example tributyltin oxide
26172-55-4,100,100,Category 1,Category 1,example CMIT (isothiazolinone)
